    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d793">

                <pb facs="1263" n="1249" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1249"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/9–2044</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Halifax</hi>)</head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to His Excellency the British
                    Ambassador and has the honor to refer to the apparent policy of the German
                    Government of treating parachutists falling into its hand as <hi
                        rendition="#italic">francs tireurs.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Reports which the American Government has received from the Supreme Headquarters,
                    Allied Expeditionary Force, indicate that atrocities have been committed against
                    Special Air Services Troops. It is understood that these airborne troops are
                    made up of American and British personnel and that the British personnel are in
                    the majority.</p>
                <p>The Government of the United States is considering addressing a strong protest to
                    the German Government with respect to the mistreatment of these soldiers. Before
                    doing so it would be interested in knowing whether the British Government would
                    join in like action with regard to this matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-20">September 20,
                            1944</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
